Body:
@OmniReality thanks for confirming the fix works on your machine too.

This is the most robust fix for this issue. The `.git` watcher was using `@parcel/watcher` to watch the entire `.git/` tree, which requires inotify and has unfixable C++ bugs when resources are exhausted. Since the VCS service only needs HEAD changes for branch tracking, watching the entire tree was unnecessary. `fs.watchFile` on `.git/HEAD` uses `stat()` syscalls instead of inotify, so it works on any filesystem regardless of inotify state. The 2-second poll interval is negligible for branch switching.

The root watcher (behind `OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_FILEWATCHER`) still uses `@parcel/watcher`. Only the always-active `.git` watcher was changed.
